  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q6_Connectivity
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: The link light on both ports is on, but the ping still fails. What
    is the most likely cause to check first?
  choices:
  - The cable is not plugged in
  - The two machines are configured on different subnets
  - The switch needs replacing
  - The cable is a cross-over rather than straight-through
  correctChoiceIndex: 1
  points: 10
  explanation: "A link light means the physical layer is good \u2014 the cable and
    ports are fine. When the wire is proved and traffic still will not pass, the
    fault has moved up to the addressing: check both with ipconfig and compare the
    network parts."
